.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_OOM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_oom \- check whether chttpsvr_req_query ran out of memory
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

bool chttpsvr_req_query_oom(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns true when an allocation for the query string of this request
failed for lack of memory.  Two allocations can fail like that: the
growth of the result array inside chttpsvr_req_query, and the shared
parse of the query string, which runs once and which
chttpsvr_req_query and chttpsvr_req_query_one start lazily on their
first use.

chttpsvr_req_query returns NULL with a count of 0 both for an absent
key and when it could not build the result array for lack of memory.
After any NULL from chttpsvr_req_query, call this function to find
out which of the two happened.

Once the flag is set it stays true for the rest of the request,
whatever query calls follow.  For a NULL req the function returns
false.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true; an allocation for the query string of this request failed out of
memory.
false; no allocation error happened, or req is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_one (3)
